WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.360
How digital payments work, and getting ready safely.

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:08.470
This is the video for module 1 of Digital Payments and POS Basics.

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:20.890
A digital payment is any payment where no cash changes hands. A number in one account goes down, and a number in another goes up. The money is real, just stored as a record.

4
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:28.460
Many people feel nervous because they cannot see the money travel. This module removes that mystery.

5
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.530
You will also learn when cash is better, and how to set up your account so it stays yours.

6
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:48.710
For example, Chioma in Enugu owes her tailor, Ada, 7,500 naira. She opens her banking app, taps Transfer, types Ada's 10-digit account number and chooses Ada's bank.

7
00:00:49.960 --> 00:01:02.480
The app shows the name ADA N. OKAFOR. This is called a name enquiry, and it is your most important safety check. If the name is not who you expect, stop. Close enough is not enough.

8
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.380
Chioma enters her 4-digit PIN. Her bank checks she has enough money.

9
00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:16.310
The network, the shared road between banks, carries the message. In Nigeria the main one is run by NIBSS.

10
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:26.900
Ada's bank adds 7,500 naira to her account, and both women get alerts. If any step fails, your own bank should reverse the debit.

11
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:37.560
Ada does not trust a screenshot. She opens her own app and sees the 7,500 naira in her balance. That is the only real proof.

12
00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.650
Chioma keeps her receipt and the session ID, a long number she will need if anything goes wrong.

13
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:54.840
Anyone can edit a picture of a receipt, and SMS alerts can be faked. When you receive money, check your own balance before you release goods or give change.

14
00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:04.920
Digital payments give you control, reach, less cash on the road, and records. Your transaction history is a free notebook that keeps itself.

15
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:17.520
Ngozi's app shows 38,000, then 41,500, then 29,000, then 45,500 naira received by transfer.

16
00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:26.090
That is 154,000 naira for the month. Her cash sales? She cannot tell, because she wrote nothing down.

17
00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.600
A statement like this can prove your income to a lender.

18
00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:37.400
Cash is not free. For example, Amina in Kaduna must pay a rice wholesaler 80,000 naira.

19
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:51.310
In cash, a POS agent charges to withdraw it, say 1,600 naira in this practice example, plus 1,000 for transport. 2,600 in all, and the risk of carrying cash.

20
00:02:52.560 --> 00:03:04.620
By transfer, her screen shows a practice charge of 50 naira, plus the same transport. That is 1,050, with a record. Always read the real fee on your screen before you confirm.

21
00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:14.080
A bank app needs a smartphone and data. A USSD code works on any phone with no data, so it is your backup when data runs out.

22
00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:22.310
Your card works at a POS or ATM without data. Wallets, QR codes and links need internet.

23
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:29.910
They are all doors into the same account. Anyone who gets through one door with your PIN can reach the whole balance.

24
00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:42.230
Open the account in your own name, with your own active phone number. If an old SIM is linked, change it at the bank, because OTPs go to whoever has that number now.

25
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:49.780
Install the app yourself, from the Play Store or App Store, and check the publisher is the real company.

26
00:03:51.030 --> 00:04:03.210
Choose a 4-digit PIN that is not your birth year, phone number, or a pattern like 1234 or 0000. Do not write it on your card.

27
00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:12.950
Turn on alerts for every transaction, check your account level and limits in the app, and save your bank's customer care number from the back of your card.

28
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:25.720
Your account number is safe to share. Your PIN, password and OTP are never shared with anyone, including someone who says they work for your bank, or a husband or close friend.

29
00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:42.820
To remember. Check the name before you confirm. Your own balance is the only true proof. Read the fee on the screen before you pay. Large or distant payments are usually safer by transfer. And keep your PIN private, even within the family.

30
00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:52.410
Draw the journey of your last payment, list which payments you can move from cash, compare one real payment, and complete your setup checklist.

31
00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.700
Continue with the lessons below.
